<title>USA: NORDIC SKIING-RESULTS OF WORLD CUP NORDIC COMBINED.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-RESULTS OF WORLD CUP NORDIC COMBINED.</headline>
<dateline>STEAMBOAT SPRINGS, Colorado 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading</p>
<p>finishers in a Nordic combined World Cup event after Sunday's</p>
<p>two-man sprint relay at Romick Rodeo Arena (120-metre</p>
<p>jumping/15-km skiing placings)</p>
<p>1. Norway-3 (Trond Einar Elden/Baard Joergen Elden) (12/1)</p>
<p>2. Norway-1 (Bjarte Engen Vik/Halldor Skard) 33.4 seconds</p>
<p>back (7/2)</p>
<p>3. Austria-1 (Felix Gottwald/Mario Stecher) 50.5 (4/6)</p>
<p>4. Finland-1 (Jari Mantila/Sampaa Lajunen) 50.8 (1/8)</p>
<p>5. Finland-2 (Topi Sarparanta/Hannu Manninen) 1:16.7 (8/4)</p>
<p>6. France-1 (Sylvain Guillaume/Fabrice Guy) 1:42.0 (9/7)</p>
<p>7. Czech-1 (Milan Kucera/Ladislav Rygl) 1:51.9 (10/5)</p>
<p>8. Japan-1 (Futoshi Otake/Kenji Ogiwara) 2:13.9 (3/9)</p>
<p>9. Norway-2 (Fred Boerre Lundberg/Knut Tore Apeland) 2:27.6</p>
<p>(19/3)</p>
<p>10. USA-1 (Tim Tetreault/Todd Lodwick) 2:24.0 (2/11)</p>
<p>Nations Cup (after three events)</p>
<p>1. Norway 1,390 points</p>
<p>2. Finland 752</p>
<p>3. Austria 351</p>
<p>4. United States 334</p>
<p>6. Japan 285</p>
<p>7. Czech Republic 238</p>
<p>8. Germany 202</p>
<p>9. Switzerland 140</p>
<p>10. Italy 54</p>
</text>
